/-!
# The natural quotient and complete opposite-core transfer

The literal Q and N=(W∩Wʸ)V have N≤Q, relative normality, an elementary
quotient and Φ(Q)≤N. The original I-action descends through its marked
SL₂ epimorphism; complementary root fixed spaces give natural coordinates
and the individual-root fixed-factor identities on this same quotient.

The original Cartan supplies every scalar on the opposite plane. A
nonidentity scalar gives C_Q(X₁)≤N. The full opposite-point stabilizer
takes X₁ to an O₂(I)-conjugate, and therefore preserves [Q,X₁].
Concrete point-radical transitivity gives M₁=L₁ N_M₁(V₁ʸ), with no
abstract orbit-transitivity premise. The actual Frattini and commutator
conditions apply 11.5.6(4--5), proving Q≤O₂(G₁). Three actual L₁-conjugate
pairs and the genuine multiplier identity give O₂(L)≤O₂(G₁), also at q=4.

Only the preceding source geometry, 11.5.6 conclusions, and radical-action
outputs remain explicit. Their discharge and the later characteristic-block
and terminal arguments belong to qt-d-1222-natural-closure-sp4.
Source: Aschbacher--Smith 11.5.7, printed p.783.
-/
